Stability
- Fix the real-device closet crash (生活 → 衣橱): a JVM circular class-init bug —
  the first static touch of the family was TopLevel.Closet.INSTANCE, whose <clinit>
  chain ran TopLevel.Companion.<clinit>, which read Closet.INSTANCE back while its
  own clinit was still on the stack, permanently capturing a null inside entries.
  Both companion lists (TopLevel.entries, LifeDestination.tabs) now build lazily;
  pinned by TopLevelEntriesTest in the exact crash order, plus ClosetSmokeTest
  (Robolectric+Compose) walking launch → 生活 → 衣橱 on a fresh install end to end.
- Drop enableMultiInstanceInvalidation(): single-process, single-instance app —
  the cross-instance broadcast bought nothing and cost a service bind on every DB open.
- Debug-only local crash journal (LifeCrashLog): uncaught exceptions write
  filesDir/debug/last_crash.txt (time/OS/app/thread/stack), chained to the previous
  handler; 我的 gains a debug-only copy/clear block; release has no trace of it.

Version & install system
- versionName 0.2.0; versionCode = VERSION_BASE(200000) + CI_BUILD_NUMBER (local: 0).
- applicationId com.xiaoming.closie → com.qq.closie — the FINAL rename, frozen forever.
- App label Closie → Life OS.
- ONE Android workflow. .github/workflows/android.yml absorbs the whole v0.2 build
  contract (JDK 17, testDebugUnitTest, assembleDebug, CI_BUILD_NUMBER, fixed signing,
  versioned APK artifact, test-report artifact) and the separately added Life OS
  workflow is removed — two workflows running the same two tasks would double every
  PR build for zero signal. Fixed signing requires ALL FOUR secrets
  (ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64 / _PASSWORD / _ALIAS / ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD); a partially
  configured keystore is treated as absent so assemble can never fail on a missing
  alias. Artifact path is the versioned wildcard with if-no-files-found: error.
- APKs are named LifeOS-v<version>-build<versionCode>.apk.

UI calibration
- Window insets: the Life shell's Scaffold is the single system-bar inset owner and
  consumes its padding; per-screen statusBarsPadding removed; Closie's inner M3 Scaffold
  no longer double-pads. Status bar → first line lands at 16–20dp.
- LifeDimensions: compact(<400dp)/regular page rhythm; LifeSpace keeps only
  component-level semantics.
- Home header: Life OS (Brand) → date line → motto, spec rhythm via blockGap.
- Empty states tightened and darkened (EmptyTitle 20sp TextSecondary).
- 生活 directory: LifeType.ModuleTitle (Serif 500 21sp) replaces PageTitle for the seven
  module rows — a peer list is not seven 26sp headlines — and the gap under 生活 is
  blockGap (≈20dp compact) instead of a fixed 32dp.
- Timeline records get a ··· menu → 删除 confirm dialog → CaptureRepository.delete(id),
  Flow-refreshed; covered by delete_existingCapture_removesIt / delete_missingCapture_doesNotCrash.

Typography
- Bundled faces under res/font (OFL/Apache, licenses in res/raw/font_licenses.txt):
  Noto Serif SC (subset static 500/600 — serif roles render fixed UI strings only),
  Noto Sans SC variable (full charset; 300/400/500 pinned via FontVariation — the only
  face user text can touch), Caveat variable (English-only decoration), Special Elite
  (numbers/timestamps/build info). System theme fonts (vivo) cannot reach any Life OS
  glyph: every role resolves inside the APK.
- Latin-only containment: Special Elite and Caveat are never handed Chinese. Home and
  timeline metadata split the HH:mm stamp (typewriter) from the Chinese source/status
  words (Sans) into separate Text runs, and LifeMetaText refuses a mono style for text
  containing CJK — no glyph relies on system fallback. Pinned by LifeFontRulesTest.
- LifeMaterialTypography: MaterialTheme now receives a typography whose every role binds
  to Serif/Sans, so a Material component we did not style still cannot reach
  FontFamily.Default (= the device theme font). This is the theme-level safety net
  under the LifeType convention.
- LifeFonts (Serif/Sans/Hand/Typewriter) + LifeType (15 roles) + LifeTypographyPreview
  specimen; Home/Timeline/Life/Profile previews all cover 360x800, 393x852, 411x891.
- APK size: fonts add ~15.2MB inside the APK (24.29MB source, DEFLATE 37–46%);
  v0.2.0 code itself adds only ~41KB over v0.1.
